# RealityAnchor — environment
#
# The analysis behind the flow (distortion, risk, node details) is generated by
# a REAL model when one is configured. With no credentials it falls back to the
# offline keyword heuristic — intended for local dev / testing only.
#
# Provider resolution (first match wins):
#   1. ANTHROPIC_API_KEY  → first-party Claude API
#   2. AWS creds          → Claude via Amazon Bedrock (on-theme for Alexa+)
#   3. neither            → heuristic fallback

# --- Option 1: first-party Claude API ---
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-...

# --- Option 2: Amazon Bedrock ---
# AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID=...
# AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=...
# AWS_REGION=us-west-2

# Optional model override. Defaults: "claude-opus-4-8" (first-party) or
# "anthropic.claude-opus-4-8" (Bedrock — note the anthropic. prefix). Set this
# if your Bedrock account has a different model enabled,
# e.g. anthropic.claude-sonnet-4-6
# REALITY_ANCHOR_MODEL=

# Public base URL of this deployment (optional).
# NEXT_PUBLIC_BASE_URL=http://localhost:3000
